invariant: INV-4
file: drbg.c
catches: drbg_test
reason: ch_drbg_seed copies the first 32 seed bytes into the key instead
  of hashing the whole seed, so every source an image concatenates after
  the first 32 bytes adds nothing, and an image that puts a public or
  cloned source first seeds from that source alone. The known answers in
  bin/drbg_test, computed with Python's hashlib and two ChaCha20
  implementations outside the tree, refuse the copied key.

--- old
    sha256 s;
    sha256_init(&s);
    sha256_update(&s, seed, seed_len);
    sha256_final(&s, g_key);
    ct_wipe(&s, sizeof s);
--- new
    for (size_t i = 0; i < CHACHA20_KEY; i++) {
        g_key[i] = seed[i];
    }
